<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pā^trae</span></b> , ārum,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πάτραι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a very ancient city in
				Achaia</i>, <i>on the promontory of Rhium</i>,
			the mod. <i>Patras</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				7, 28, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 17, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 1, 2</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				27, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 4,
				5, § 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
				417</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pā^trensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Patrœ</i>, <i>Patrœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyso Patrensis,</span>”
				<i>of Patrœ</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 13, 19, 1 sq.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bibliotheca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					18, 9, 5</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pătren-ses</span></b> ,
			ĭum, m., <i>the
				Patrœans</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Patrensium leges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 13, 19, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
